# Compton profile shell occupancies
#
# Number of electrons in each atomic subshell for which G4EMLOW tabulates a
# Compton profile, in the order the profiles appear in profile-<Z>.dat.
#
# Source: F. Biggs, L. B. Mendelsohn and J. B. Mann, "Hartree-Fock Compton
# profiles for the elements", At. Data Nucl. Data Tables 16, 201-309 (1975),
# as tabulated in the DABAX file ComptonProfiles.dat (#UOCCUP keyword), from
# https://github.com/oasys-kit/DabaxFiles at commit 70ff903 (MIT licence).
# The DABAX profiles are identical to G4EMLOW profile-<Z>.dat to all tabulated
# digits for Z = 1-100, and its #UOCCUP is aligned column-for-column with
# them, so these occupancies refer to the same subshell as each profile.
#
# The occupancies in G4EMLOW shell-doppler.dat cannot be used: they follow the
# ordering of Geant4 G4AtomicShells (subshells sorted by decreasing binding
# energy) rather than the (n, l, j) ordering of the profiles and of the
# binding energies in the same file. For Z = 43 and 59-92 the two orderings
# differ and the occupancy does not belong to the subshell it is paired with.
#
# j0 is the profile value at pz = 0, carried as a fingerprint so that
# make_compton.py can verify each occupancy is still matched to the profile it
# was derived against.
#
#   Z  shell  electrons        j0
    1      1          1          0.849
    2      1          2          0.535
    3      1          2          0.329
    3      2          1           1.94
    4      1          2          0.237
    4      2          2           1.34
